-- title:
--   Frequently Bounded Approximations Lie In The Closure Domain
-- statement:
--   This theorem applies the closed-graph selection principle to a closable partially defined linear map.
--
--   Let $X$ be a real normed space, let $H$ be a complete real Hilbert space, and let $T:X\dashrightarrow H$ be a closable partial linear map. Let $x\in X$ and let $(f_n)$ be an approximating sequence for $x$ in the pre-energy generated by $T$. Assume that for some $L\in[0,\infty)$, represented by `NNReal`,
--
--   $$
--   \|T f_n\|\le L
--   $$
--
--   holds frequently along $n\to\infty$. Then $x$ belongs to the domain of the closure $\overline T$, and the closure value obeys
--
--   $$
--   \|\overline T(x)\|\le L.
--   $$
--
--   The declaration is `mem_closure_domain_of_frequently`. The norm bound is stated using the nonnegative norm `nnnorm`; the conclusion includes both domain membership and the corresponding bound.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Energy/Relaxation/LinearPMap.lean#L316-L335 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.Relaxation.LinearPMap`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.PreEnergy.mem_closure_domain_of_frequently`; the repository is private at upload time).

